    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class (the other files are support classes), and `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `membershipNumber` field on `Owner`, formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>` where `YY` is the last two digits of the `registrationDate` year (e.g. `SMI-0007-M26`).\n\nFollowing the existing pattern for the other derived, read-only owner fields (`displayName`, `initials`):\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `membershipNumber` property to the `Owner` schema (so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field).\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 mapped it via a MapStruct expression backed by a `membershipNumber(Owner)` helper that composes `customerCode` + `\"-M\"` + the zero-padded two-digit year (`getYear() % 100`, `%02d`). It returns `null` when either source field is absent, which keeps GETs on seed owners (whose `customer_code`/`registration_date` columns are unset) from NPEing.\n\nComputing it in the mapper means it's derived from the owner's own fields at serialization time \u2014 seed-independent, and correct on both the create response and subsequent fetches, exactly as the acceptance test expects.",
